From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Studio Local Patches <local-patches@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(usage): per-model-call context accounting; carry misc
 drift

Coding-agent proxy runs record per-call usage through a per-request
observer (createProxyUsageObserver) instead of the shared handler, tag
rows with usage_scope=model_call plus the context boundary (history
revision and native session id), and persist a session_context_usage
snapshot (table schema already introduced with 0005) so the chat context
bar reflects the latest model call - cache read/write included - instead
of near-zero lifetime billing totals. /context now uses the latest
request's context while /usage keeps accumulated totals; cleared or
rotated context boundaries stay unknown rather than showing stale
numbers.

Carried faithfully from the build tree: chat.contextUnknown translations
for nine locales, npm lockfile libc-field removals (21 blocks, npm
version drift), a run of trailing-whitespace lines in run-manager.ts and
services/index.ts, and added usage/proxy tests (context-usage-store,
proxy-request-usage, e2e context-usage and updated suites).
